MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_001: Sorry to make you wait, soldier. We're here now.\nEverything will be OK.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_002: Thank heavens... The town... You've got to...\nrescue...them...
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_003: Ngh...
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_004: You died with honor, soldier.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_005: I'll take the west side! You take the east!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_006: Battle report! Only minimal casualties amongst\nthe civilians.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_007: All thanks to your impressive entry into the\nfray, Promised One!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_008: You drew the enemy's focus, allowing our own\na moment to collect themselves.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_009: And as a result, our reinforcements made it to the\nbattle before it was too late. Truly amazing!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_010: <NCA>"Your decisiveness made a difference."
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_011: <NCB>"We still had too many deaths..."
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_012: <ACA>Thank you for noticing! Quick analysis and swift\naction are skills upon which I pride myself.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_013: <ACB>Lives were lost, to be sure.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_014: In any case, you were truly marvelous out there\ntoday, Promised One. Spectacular, really.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_015: It's the mark of a truly sterling warrior, delivering\nresults...while also caring deeply for others.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_016: I'm afraid that I just don't come close to the\nstandard you set.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_017: I'm the sort who only thinks of herself. I charge\nahead with little regard for those around me.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_018: I've come to realize how often I say things\nthoughtlessly. Always too late, after the fact.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_019: In fact, I'm feeling that a little right now. Hehe.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_020: But I do like who I am—and how I am. So I just keep\nliving for myself alone.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_021: <NCA>"But you did save people, just now."
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_022: <NCB>"But you do serve as a knight."
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_023: <ACA>I'm driven to race in gallantly, to be THE one to\nsave the weak. I love it—I really do.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_024: <ACB>A knight, yes... And I aspire to serve a worthy lord,\nracing into battle, smiting evil in their name!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_025: Really, I want to serve the noble and beautiful\nAND the great and good.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_026: That's just who I am. I suppose my ambitions, in\nessence, make me very common. Well, so be it!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_027: Why is THAT so funny? I thought we were having\na serious discussion!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_028: Hahaha! You know, I would have never let\nany of that out if you were of noble status.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_029: Well, aside from a noble lord, I still seek a perfect\ncompanion too. Where will I find either one now?
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_A_030: Perhaps all is not lost... Maybe saving the world is\nthe best way to secure myself both!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_001: Well, I helped save the world. And yet... Oh,\nPromised One. Why did this happen?
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_002: <NCA>"I'm sorry I worried you."
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_003: Hm? Oh, if it isn't you, Promised One. Still alive.\nWell, of course you are...
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_004: <NCA>"Would you...rather I be dead?"
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_005: Of course not! Not in the slightest!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_006: I'm simply lost in my thoughts, mired in despair,\nseeing what my life's come to in Dagda.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_007: I believed that, if I saved the world, my reputation\nwould shine from sea to sea.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_008: But everyone is so busy putting their lives back\ntogether that they couldn't care less about me.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_009: I never found a lord worthy of my service. And\nmy perfect partner? They've yet to appear.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_010: It's so unfair! I worked so hard! And for what?
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_011: <NCA>"Sorry. It's very unfair."
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_012: <NCB>"I care about you, at least."
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_013: <ACA>I have no one! No one at all! I mean, except you.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_014: <ACB>I suppose that's true. You did come find me, after all.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_015: YOU! You ARE here!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_016: Would you... Could you...be interested in being\nmy companion? It's a bright idea, I must say!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_017: After all, you'll always be on the move, trying to\nsave people here and there, Promised One!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_018: We both need someone to continue on with...\nTo trust—to grow old with.
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_019: <NCA>"My life is far from easy."
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_022: 
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_020: <RSDS>Who wants easy? A knight of sterling quality must\ncharge in with valor!
MID_SE_Ism_Cat_S_021: No matter the road ahead, I will rise gloriously to\nthe occasion—a Catania you'll never forget!